            {
                "entry_id": "bf8351c2-adfa-3d9e-a5ef-03b11a5a47c1",
                "word": "scheduled",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "56391151-ae6e-4db8-a54a-5734c681e0bb",
                        "entry_id": "bf8351c2-adfa-3d9e-a5ef-03b11a5a47c1",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "scheduleds"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "b2988d6c-f686-30b3-bbc3-650819e9cb00",
                        "entry_id": "bf8351c2-adfa-3d9e-a5ef-03b11a5a47c1",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Synonym of schedulee."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "informal"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ed5e6874-5427-4934-b96a-30b167752893",
                                "sense_id": "b2988d6c-f686-30b3-bbc3-650819e9cb00",
                                "text": "However, one cannot help finding some similarity between these sharp words and those which became familiar when - well before the oil crisis - the fight between the scheduleds and non-scheduleds was in full swing."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "14064ef0-11ec-4ca3-9572-3503417df122",
                                "sense_id": "b2988d6c-f686-30b3-bbc3-650819e9cb00",
                                "text": "If you have a curfew for the scheduleds, I think you should have them for the nonscheduleds, and of course in general aviation you have a wide range of corporate jet aircraft, and some of these corporate jet aircraft actually make more noise than the usual light-body airline jets, so I think it should stay the way it is."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4620ef5d-f71c-4e41-beb4-4c2b86cf2ce0",
                                "sense_id": "b2988d6c-f686-30b3-bbc3-650819e9cb00",
                                "text": "Finally, as election time approached, the Congress, in a last desperate attempt to induce backwards and scheduleds to return to the party fold, raised the overall reservation quota to 68 per cent, then 73 per cent, and finally 80 per cent."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
